import json
from pathlib import Path
h=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
s=json.loads((h/'source.json').read_text());a=json.loads((h/'source-analysis.json').read_text())['sources'];v=json.loads((h/'validation.json').read_text())
(h/'classification.md').write_text('''# Classification

Database math, lineage '''+s['lineage']+', source basis '+str(s['basis'])+'''. All 14 practice sources and the canonical example were captured in one Pull. None has been modified.

All sources are rated hard and use radio selection. Thirteen have one selection field; q-74525 has two fields with the same key and one missing key, so it is structurally ungradable and excluded. Eight sources request a vector general solution. Six request a complete 3×4 RREF matrix, of which five have complete single-field banks. The vector and matrix answer shapes are distinct templates. Row swap, pivot normalization, and elimination stage sequences further divide them; this package conservatively retains a separate backbone/profile per source, without claiming every differing number is a new template. Complete per-source parameters, matrices, fields, choices, keys and worked solutions are retained in source-analysis.json.

The supported generator contains three matrix-response templates with five complete five-option profiles (q-131632, q-74617, q-74618, q-131636, q-74621). The swap/eliminate template contains q-131632 and q-74621; the eliminate/normalize template contains q-74617 and q-131636; the eliminate-only template contains q-74618. Their profile-specific generator entry points retain source aliases. They all use pivot columns 1 and 2, a zero third row and a free z variable. q-131636 preserves a mixed math/text bank with “No solution.” The other supported banks are math matrices. Unsupported backbones remain in source evidence; no fidelity is claimed for them.

No easy or moderate source exists in this captured bank. Absence does not prove those levels mathematically impossible. They are outside this source-grounded package and remain explicit capability exceptions; new evidence reopens classification. Plot rating is none for every practice source: all mathematical displays are equations and matrices, not graphs or diagrams. The canonical example's standalone matrix SVG is typeset mathematics and is not reused by this generator.
''')
(h/'template-extraction.md').write_text('''# Template extraction

The source-analysis.json record describes every original question, field and full bank before generalization. source-replay.json maps all 25 supported source choices, including every distractor, to its exact generated value and recipe. Profiles are never pooled or partially selected.

Each supported template supplies three equations in x,y,z with a fixed coefficient matrix and a dependent third equation. The learner selects the complete reduced augmented matrix. Its solution stages are the original augmented matrix, each annotated Gauss-Jordan row operation, row echelon form with two pivots, and elimination above those pivots. Keep the original prose, answer shape, notation, field key, choice count and exact operation sequence. Coefficients, pivot positions and the complete requested matrix are fixed to preserve this conservative workload; they are not claimed to be intrinsically fixed by the KP.

Variable slot k is a nonzero integer in {-5,-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5}. Observed parameters are k=1. The explicit same-method generalization replaces every equation RHS b_i by k*b_i and every last-column value in every intermediate, final and choice matrix by k times that value. Text choices stay unchanged. E[A|k b]=[EA|k Eb] for every elementary row-operation matrix E, so the original annotations and operation sequence remain exact. Nonzero k preserves rank, consistency, option distinctness and correct designation; each of those properties is also checked independently. Scaling b changes the affine solution set. Fixed coefficient choices are a narrower policy than the KP's possible full range.

Distractor recipe for each source option: retain its complete first three columns and multiply its entire last column by k; for the text option retain “No solution.” These are observed matrix-expression patterns with a covariant extension. Their psychological interpretation is unresolved. No misconception feedback is invented. The mapping includes altered constants and compound errors exactly as complete source matrices; no recipe is replaced by a plausible alternative.

Sampling chooses a complete profile first and then k. It rejects unsupported levels/profiles/scales, has 50 validated distinct augmented row spaces, and never creates additional questions by shuffling banks or seeds. Every instance has field-owned answer UUIDs. Deduplication uses the exact augmented RREF, so equivalent equation systems, source identities and option changes do not increase inventory. The k=1 replay is fidelity evidence, not automatically fresh inventory.

Source replay matches prompt, worked solution and all five options verbatim for each supported profile (5/5 complete banks, 25/25 choices, 20/20 distractors). The other nine practice sources are excluded from generator support, including eight vector-response sources and the malformed duplicate-field source. The generator makes no full-KP fidelity claim. Review.md places exact replays beside negative and positive changed-RHS instances for every supported profile. No target-position slot is declared; the target is the complete RREF matrix.
''')
(h/'plot-extraction.md').write_text('# Plot extraction and generation\n\nNo graphs or diagrams occur in the supported templates. All matrices are inline/display LaTeX; they do not require raster plot assets. Stages 5 and 7 therefore require no plot renderer or asset publication. Source references, roles and display layout are retained in source-analysis.json.\n')
cap={'supported_levels':['hard'],'unsupported_levels':['easy','moderate'],'exceptions':[
 {'level':level,'status':'unsupported','evidence':'No observed source at this difficulty; no validated same-difficulty template in this bounded package. Not proof of impossibility; new source evidence reopens classification.','unfilled_reserve':5} for level in ('easy','moderate')],
 'bounded_domain':{'profiles':5,'scale_values':[-5,-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5],'distinct_augmented_row_spaces':v['distinct_mathematical_tasks'],'finite_limit':50,'remaining_capacity_depends_on_existing_and_shown_content':True},
 'excluded_profiles':[{'source_id':x['source_id'],'reason':x['exclusion']} for x in a if not x['supported']], 'unsupported_levels_filled':False}
(h/'capabilities.json').write_text(json.dumps(cap,indent=2)+'\n')
(h/'README.md').write_text('# Two-pivot singular 3×3 RREF inventory package\n\nGenerator: ../17592186096745.py. Run `.venv/bin/python generate/scratch/17592186096745/validate.py` for complete source-bank replay, independent exact mathematics, annotated row operations and actual native grading over all 50 bounded instances. Run `.venv/bin/python generate/scratch/17592186096745/replenish.py` for a fresh inventory check and additive basis-guarded registration/replenishment under application api.lock. Exact requests, previews, receipts, committed-basis reads and inventory checks remain under reference/replenishment.\n\nOnly hard is supported. Easy and moderate reserves remain explicitly unfilled; capabilities.json describes bounded exceptions and excluded source backbones. Originals, canonical example, learner history and unrelated KPs are preserved.\n')
